  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nA hot, dry, and breezy pattern will continue through the \nextended as southwest flow aloft persists between upper \ntroughing along/off the coast and an upper ridge over the south-\ncentral U.S. Highs Saturday will remain very hot, forecast to \nexceed 100 degrees once again in the lower valleys. Winds will \nincrease further ahead of a trough moving into western \nWashington, with widespread gusts 20-35 mph, strongest over \nhigher terrain. Additionally, relative humidity will be very low\nresulting in elevated fire weather concerns. The trough will \nbring a slight cooldown Sunday into early next week, but it will\nstill be hot and dry with lower valleys reaching the mid 90s. \nWinds will subside after Saturday, but it will still be breezy \neach afternoon. Dry air will keep shower and thunderstorm \nchances less than 10%.",
